1
00:00:18,955 --> 00:00:20,274
I accidentally saw you.

2
00:00:20,275 --> 00:00:21,115
Huh?

3
00:00:21,175 --> 00:00:22,145
Saw what?

4
00:00:22,145 --> 00:00:23,145
Huh?

5
00:00:23,185 --> 00:00:26,855
Never mind.
I thought I forgot my drumsticks.

6
00:00:26,915 --> 00:00:28,655
And then I saw you two...

7
00:00:32,025 --> 00:00:33,255
Mikkun.

8
00:00:33,695 --> 00:00:35,594
Actually, we're...

9
00:00:35,595 --> 00:00:36,915
Oh, man.

10
00:00:37,625 --> 00:00:38,835
Sorry about that.

11
00:00:38,925 --> 00:00:40,535
Sorry you had to see something so weird.

12
00:00:40,695 --> 00:00:42,095
I was the one who started it.

13
00:00:43,305 --> 00:00:44,804
Sorry. It's gross, right?

14
00:00:44,805 --> 00:00:46,994
No, not at all.

15
00:00:46,995 --> 00:00:48,535
It is gross, isn't it?

16
00:01:23,795 --> 00:01:31,295
"How Do We Relationship?"

17
00:01:36,195 --> 00:01:39,595
(Episode 2: This Must Be Love)

18
00:01:39,615 --> 00:01:41,425
Why did you say that just now?

19
00:01:43,325 --> 00:01:46,225
I didn't like the way you said that.

20
00:01:47,255 --> 00:01:51,035
Why make it sound like you
forced yourself on me or something?

21
00:01:52,205 --> 00:01:54,974
And calling it gross?
That's going too far.

22
00:01:54,975 --> 00:01:56,005
Well...

23
00:01:58,515 --> 00:02:01,145
People are going to say mean things anyway.

24
00:02:03,295 --> 00:02:07,855
If that's the case, saying it
first makes it hurt less, right?

25
00:02:09,285 --> 00:02:10,775
Is that so?

26
00:02:12,325 --> 00:02:14,295
But Mikkun wouldn't do that, would he?

27
00:02:14,415 --> 00:02:15,515
He's a nice guy.

28
00:02:16,295 --> 00:02:17,995
And you two are pretty close.

29
00:02:18,925 --> 00:02:21,095
That has nothing to do
with how close we are.

30
00:02:23,175 --> 00:02:26,065
Don't you trust your own friends?

31
00:02:26,975 --> 00:02:28,675
Miwa, you're...

32
00:02:30,905 --> 00:02:32,615
Never mind. It's nothing.

33
00:02:33,445 --> 00:02:34,715
Huh? What is it?

34
00:02:35,215 --> 00:02:36,215
By the way.

35
00:02:36,715 --> 00:02:38,184
Have you gotten more assertive lately?

36
00:02:38,185 --> 00:02:39,815
Were you always like this, Miwa?

37
00:02:40,985 --> 00:02:42,615
How should I put it?

38
00:02:43,655 --> 00:02:44,755
Hmm...

39
00:02:46,425 --> 00:02:49,425
Maybe it's because I'm not alone anymore.

40
00:02:50,815 --> 00:02:52,365
What does that mean?

41
00:02:52,395 --> 00:02:54,395
Are you writing poetry?

42
00:02:54,495 --> 00:02:55,665
Are you a poet or something?

43
00:02:56,165 --> 00:02:58,965
- Oh, great poet!
- I told you I'm not.

44
00:03:00,335 --> 00:03:05,445
Didn't I say something before
about living freely and without restraints?

45
00:03:05,945 --> 00:03:07,245
So lame.

46
00:03:10,055 --> 00:03:14,785
All right. I'll go explain
things to Mikkun.

47
00:03:15,955 --> 00:03:17,355
I want to go too.

48
00:03:17,755 --> 00:03:20,395
It's fine.
I'll just go by myself.

49
00:03:21,325 --> 00:03:23,695
Then give me a good luck kiss.

50
00:03:23,735 --> 00:03:25,301
That'll give me the strength to do my best.

51
00:03:25,325 --> 00:03:26,335
Kiss, kiss.

52
00:03:26,555 --> 00:03:28,204
Mwah, mwah, mwah, mwah!

53
00:03:28,205 --> 00:03:29,705
No, stop it!

54
00:03:29,935 --> 00:03:31,204
We're outside!

55
00:03:31,205 --> 00:03:34,305
Aw, Miwa, you're so stingy.

56
00:03:35,375 --> 00:03:36,475
Whatever. It's fine.

57
00:03:37,205 --> 00:03:38,445
I'm taking off.

58
00:03:47,175 --> 00:03:48,155
Saeko.

59
00:03:48,155 --> 00:03:49,155
Yeah?

60
00:03:51,885 --> 00:03:54,425
You're so bold...

61
00:03:55,755 --> 00:03:57,625
You're the one who told me to kiss you.

62
00:03:59,195 --> 00:04:00,195
Thanks.

63
00:04:00,395 --> 00:04:01,795
Now I can do my best.

64
00:04:08,935 --> 00:04:11,805
And I ended up putting
it off until today...

65
00:04:13,735 --> 00:04:15,495
I'm so nervous.

66
00:04:15,515 --> 00:04:17,135
This is scary.

67
00:04:18,385 --> 00:04:19,495
- Yo!
- Oh.

68
00:04:19,555 --> 00:04:20,615
What are you doing?

69
00:04:22,455 --> 00:04:23,985
Mikkun.

70
00:04:25,035 --> 00:04:27,395
What do you really think about
what happened the other day?

71
00:04:27,925 --> 00:04:30,615
Honestly, it really startled me.

72
00:04:30,625 --> 00:04:32,625
Imagine if you suddenly
saw me kissing someone.

73
00:04:32,795 --> 00:04:34,535
You'd definitely be shocked.

74
00:04:35,835 --> 00:04:36,835
True...

75
00:04:38,855 --> 00:04:40,675
By the way, are you two dating?

76
00:04:43,035 --> 00:04:44,205
You could say that...

77
00:04:48,325 --> 00:04:50,985
- Here.
- Thanks...

78
00:04:59,315 --> 00:05:00,995
Oh, I see.

79
00:05:03,155 --> 00:05:04,735
Huh? That's it?

80
00:05:04,765 --> 00:05:06,541
Don't you have anything
else to say? Be honest.

81
00:05:06,565 --> 00:05:07,565
Like what?

82
00:05:07,665 --> 00:05:10,065
Like... it's gross, or there's no way.

83
00:05:10,105 --> 00:05:11,611
Or that you're physically repulsed by it.

84
00:05:11,635 --> 00:05:15,505
What? Do I have to
think of you like that?

85
00:05:15,705 --> 00:05:18,775
I was surprised, sure,
but it's no big deal.

86
00:05:18,835 --> 00:05:21,045
I just thought, "Oh, okay." That's all.

87
00:05:21,475 --> 00:05:23,235
That's probably how
most people would react.

88
00:05:23,645 --> 00:05:27,315
Now I suddenly don't know what to say...

89
00:05:27,585 --> 00:05:30,125
Did someone actually
say those things to you?

90
00:05:30,155 --> 00:05:31,561
If there's a jerk like that out there,

91
00:05:31,585 --> 00:05:33,625
- I'll go teach them a lesson...
- No, there isn't!

92
00:05:43,805 --> 00:05:44,805
It's just that...

93
00:05:45,835 --> 00:05:49,275
when people found out I was
dating a girl in middle school,

94
00:05:49,905 --> 00:05:51,375
the word spread.

95
00:05:52,575 --> 00:05:55,315
It wasn't so much me,
but the girl I was dating who had it worse.

96
00:05:55,415 --> 00:05:58,685
People said a lot of awful things to her
and did some really mean stuff.

97
00:06:00,955 --> 00:06:03,555
I just don't want Miwa to go through that.

98
00:06:06,525 --> 00:06:08,325
Don't worry about it.

99
00:06:08,495 --> 00:06:11,425
I'm on Saeko and Miwa's side.

100
00:06:11,695 --> 00:06:12,695
Right?

101
00:06:13,365 --> 00:06:15,035
Ouch!

102
00:06:15,135 --> 00:06:17,075
- You hit me for real just now!
- No, I didn't!

103
00:06:17,105 --> 00:06:18,105
That was close.

104
00:06:18,335 --> 00:06:20,305
My arm is going to break!

105
00:06:21,495 --> 00:06:22,495
You jerk!

106
00:06:23,945 --> 00:06:24,945
Hey, so...

107
00:06:26,315 --> 00:06:29,475
We're actually dating.

108
00:06:31,415 --> 00:06:32,415
Huh?

109
00:06:36,355 --> 00:06:39,254
Oh, really? Congratulations!

110
00:06:39,255 --> 00:06:40,255
Huh?

111
00:06:40,325 --> 00:06:41,825
- You already knew?
- Yeah, I knew.

112
00:06:41,855 --> 00:06:43,055
Seriously?

113
00:06:47,665 --> 00:06:49,065
Um... so...

114
00:06:49,675 --> 00:06:50,675
Uh...

115
00:06:52,565 --> 00:06:55,135
Tsu... Tsuruta-kun?

116
00:06:56,275 --> 00:06:58,845
Ah, so you like Miwa...

117
00:06:59,475 --> 00:07:00,645
I see.

118
00:07:00,695 --> 00:07:02,614
Tsuruta is heartbroken!

119
00:07:02,615 --> 00:07:03,984
That's gotta hurt.

120
00:07:03,985 --> 00:07:04,985
It's fine, it's fine.

121
00:07:04,986 --> 00:07:06,825
You don't get it at all.

122
00:07:31,075 --> 00:07:34,715
Miwa, are you still looking at that?

123
00:07:34,975 --> 00:07:36,815
Let's hurry up and go to the next spot.

124
00:07:37,335 --> 00:07:39,615
By the way, I suddenly have
a craving for a seafood bowl.

125
00:07:40,115 --> 00:07:43,484
Can't you appreciate
the atmosphere a little?

126
00:07:43,485 --> 00:07:44,655
We're at an aquarium!

127
00:07:44,695 --> 00:07:47,295
It's our one-month anniversary date!

128
00:07:47,675 --> 00:07:50,395
How am I supposed to set
the mood looking at fish?

129
00:07:50,415 --> 00:07:51,525
And it smells like fish.

130
00:07:52,565 --> 00:07:54,195
What do you mean, it smells?

131
00:07:54,235 --> 00:07:56,575
Honestly, I'm ignoring you, Saeko.

132
00:07:56,805 --> 00:07:59,265
Don't be mad.

133
00:08:01,275 --> 00:08:04,404
All right, put that away.
Food's here.

134
00:08:04,405 --> 00:08:05,854
Thank you.

135
00:08:05,855 --> 00:08:08,914
- Here.
- Wow, the tuna looks delicious!

136
00:08:08,915 --> 00:08:10,845
- Looks great, right?
- Yeah!

137
00:08:12,455 --> 00:08:17,394
- So, once again, happy...
- One-month anniversary!

138
00:08:17,395 --> 00:08:19,425
Let's eat!

139
00:08:31,535 --> 00:08:33,035
So good!

140
00:08:38,505 --> 00:08:39,745
Hey, Miwa.

141
00:08:40,015 --> 00:08:41,615
What exactly do you like about me?

142
00:08:42,275 --> 00:08:43,145
Huh?

143
00:08:43,285 --> 00:08:44,385
What do I like...

144
00:08:45,145 --> 00:08:46,184
Why ask that all of a sudden?

145
00:08:46,185 --> 00:08:48,136
Doesn't it feel like an anniversary
thing to do? Asking questions like this.

146
00:08:49,355 --> 00:08:50,355
Hmm...

147
00:08:51,355 --> 00:08:52,755
How energetic you are?

148
00:08:53,655 --> 00:08:54,755
Huh? What?

149
00:08:54,795 --> 00:08:56,795
A comment on an elementary
schooler's report card?

150
00:08:57,525 --> 00:09:03,605
Then what do you like about me, Saeko?

151
00:09:03,835 --> 00:09:05,035
Huh?

152
00:09:05,615 --> 00:09:06,975
Hmm...

153
00:09:08,475 --> 00:09:09,495
Everything?

154
00:09:09,645 --> 00:09:11,775
That's such a cop-out!

155
00:09:11,805 --> 00:09:13,034
No, it's not.

156
00:09:13,035 --> 00:09:13,775
It totally is.

157
00:09:13,776 --> 00:09:14,895
I'm telling the truth!

158
00:09:14,915 --> 00:09:17,214
As punishment,
I'm confiscating a piece of tuna.

159
00:09:17,215 --> 00:09:19,035
Hey, wait!

160
00:09:20,385 --> 00:09:22,655
I swear, I can't win with you.

161
00:09:30,795 --> 00:09:34,635
Saeko, have you been
acting a little weird today?

162
00:09:35,565 --> 00:09:37,865
Like, unusually sweet or something?

163
00:09:38,855 --> 00:09:39,855
Huh?

164
00:09:39,975 --> 00:09:42,335
I'm always sweet, okay?

165
00:09:47,545 --> 00:09:48,545
So good.

166
00:09:50,775 --> 00:09:52,955
Time really flies when you're having fun.

167
00:09:53,815 --> 00:09:55,255
Yeah.

168
00:09:56,455 --> 00:09:57,455
So cute.

169
00:10:03,925 --> 00:10:04,925
Huh?

170
00:10:04,965 --> 00:10:06,465
We don't go this way, do we?

171
00:10:06,955 --> 00:10:07,974
Huh?

172
00:10:07,975 --> 00:10:09,705
No, it's this way.

173
00:10:09,735 --> 00:10:10,735
No, it's not.

174
00:10:11,465 --> 00:10:13,005
The station is over there.

175
00:10:13,605 --> 00:10:14,605
No...

176
00:10:14,835 --> 00:10:16,035
Um...

177
00:10:21,135 --> 00:10:23,845
I want to go in here.

178
00:10:29,255 --> 00:10:31,255
This is...

179
00:10:33,155 --> 00:10:34,315
I want to do it.

180
00:10:34,655 --> 00:10:36,135
I want to do it with you today, Miwa.

181
00:10:39,255 --> 00:10:40,255
Huh?

182
00:10:40,635 --> 00:10:42,665
Isn't this way too fast?

183
00:10:42,735 --> 00:10:44,435
We've only been dating for a month.

184
00:10:44,465 --> 00:10:46,035
It's already been a month.

185
00:10:46,075 --> 00:10:48,475
I feel like I've waited long enough.

186
00:10:50,705 --> 00:10:55,275
Anyway, today...
I'm just not mentally prepared for this...

187
00:10:55,475 --> 00:10:56,915
Then when will you be ready?

188
00:10:57,815 --> 00:10:58,815
Uh...

189
00:10:59,375 --> 00:11:02,015
When... um...

190
00:11:09,895 --> 00:11:10,995
I get it.

191
00:11:11,325 --> 00:11:12,765
Let's just forget about it today.

192
00:11:12,935 --> 00:11:13,995
Let's go home.

193
00:11:16,955 --> 00:11:18,835
I'm sorry...

194
00:11:18,865 --> 00:11:20,134
It's fine.

195
00:11:20,135 --> 00:11:22,695
Besides, this isn't something
you should be apologizing for.

196
00:11:22,755 --> 00:11:23,755
Let's go.

197
00:11:28,915 --> 00:11:32,715
And so, we just went home that day.

198
00:11:33,715 --> 00:11:37,784
How long do normal couples date

199
00:11:37,785 --> 00:11:39,995
before they do that kind of thing?

200
00:11:41,055 --> 00:11:42,555
Hmm...

201
00:11:43,055 --> 00:11:47,365
Personally, I'd totally do it even
if we weren't officially dating.

202
00:11:47,715 --> 00:11:50,535
Okay, okay. There are definitely
people like you out there...

203
00:11:50,765 --> 00:11:54,535
But there's no rule saying you
have to wait a few months, right?

204
00:11:54,655 --> 00:11:56,634
You should just do it
when both of you want to.

205
00:11:56,635 --> 00:11:59,555
But we're talking about Saeko here.

206
00:11:59,635 --> 00:12:02,544
Can she really hold back?

207
00:12:02,545 --> 00:12:03,035
Huh?

208
00:12:03,036 --> 00:12:06,035
I feel like Saeko would
make a move pretty quickly.

209
00:12:06,215 --> 00:12:09,984
Besides, if it were me, if I couldn't
have sex with the person I like,

210
00:12:09,985 --> 00:12:13,355
then there'd be no point in dating.

211
00:12:13,695 --> 00:12:15,595
No point in dating...

212
00:12:15,695 --> 00:12:16,795
Hey, Rika.

213
00:12:17,025 --> 00:12:19,341
If it were me, I'd want to touch
them as long as I like them.

214
00:12:19,365 --> 00:12:23,135
After all, you want to get to know
them better through sex, right?

215
00:12:23,765 --> 00:12:24,824
Huh? You guys don't feel that way?

216
00:12:24,825 --> 00:12:25,705
No way.

217
00:12:25,706 --> 00:12:27,475
Why not? You definitely would.

218
00:12:27,505 --> 00:12:28,505
I...

219
00:12:29,165 --> 00:12:32,205
Did I trample all over Saeko's feelings?

220
00:12:33,025 --> 00:12:36,214
Um... That's just my
personal opinion, okay?

221
00:12:36,215 --> 00:12:38,785
I'm the worst.

222
00:12:45,685 --> 00:12:47,371
We should definitely
go to the beach, right?

223
00:12:47,395 --> 00:12:49,425
Wait, you don't have other plans, do you?

224
00:12:49,865 --> 00:12:51,095
Yeah... I guess.

225
00:12:51,125 --> 00:12:53,195
I really want to go to the beach.

226
00:12:54,535 --> 00:12:57,035
But I heard the summer
training camp is mandatory.

227
00:12:59,675 --> 00:13:00,575
You're kidding, right?

228
00:13:00,575 --> 00:13:01,425
I'm serious.

229
00:13:01,426 --> 00:13:03,775
Whoa, seriously?

230
00:13:03,985 --> 00:13:07,645
I was planning to go on a trip
with my girlfriend. Now that's ruined.

231
00:13:07,715 --> 00:13:10,045
Huh? You have a girlfriend, Lucha?

232
00:13:11,445 --> 00:13:13,984
As a matter of fact, I do!

233
00:13:13,985 --> 00:13:14,985
Wanna see?

234
00:13:15,365 --> 00:13:17,385
- Nope.
- Come on, just look.

235
00:13:17,425 --> 00:13:18,665
- No... That's too close.
- Look closely.

236
00:13:18,685 --> 00:13:20,795
Come on, come on, take a look.

237
00:13:20,845 --> 00:13:21,845
See?

238
00:13:23,665 --> 00:13:24,785
How have things been lately?

239
00:13:25,065 --> 00:13:28,795
Has Saeko been all lovey-dovey lately?

240
00:13:29,505 --> 00:13:31,835
We're doing pretty
well. Just normal, I guess.

241
00:13:33,205 --> 00:13:39,045
But... lately it feels like
we're a bit out of sync.

242
00:13:39,715 --> 00:13:40,545
Huh?

243
00:13:40,665 --> 00:13:42,465
Like the attempted sex
incident, for example.

244
00:13:42,545 --> 00:13:44,485
Attempted sex incident!?

245
00:13:45,045 --> 00:13:46,515
What the heck are you doing?

246
00:13:46,815 --> 00:13:49,204
Is this something we should be hearing?

247
00:13:49,205 --> 00:13:51,855
It doesn't matter.
It's not a big deal anyway.

248
00:13:52,255 --> 00:13:56,565
It's just... I feel like we're
being too polite to each other.

249
00:13:57,965 --> 00:13:59,165
You see, Miwa...

250
00:13:59,465 --> 00:14:04,505
Whenever she's trying to read my mood, she
stares at me with these total puppy-dog eyes.

251
00:14:05,465 --> 00:14:06,475
How should I put it?

252
00:14:06,505 --> 00:14:10,045
It makes me feel like
I've done something wrong.

253
00:14:14,765 --> 00:14:22,285
Saeko, don't tell me you
find Miwa a bit annoying?

254
00:14:23,785 --> 00:14:26,854
No, no, no, not at all.

255
00:14:26,855 --> 00:14:27,994
- It's not to that extent...
- I get it, I get it.

256
00:14:27,995 --> 00:14:28,795
- No, no.
- Totally get it.

257
00:14:28,795 --> 00:14:29,795
Ah, Miwa.

258
00:14:33,395 --> 00:14:35,865
Mi... Miwa.

259
00:14:36,985 --> 00:14:37,985
Miwa...

260
00:14:38,535 --> 00:14:40,205
Did you hear that just now?

261
00:14:41,135 --> 00:14:42,335
I heard it...

262
00:14:43,465 --> 00:14:46,675
You think I'm annoying, right?

263
00:14:48,125 --> 00:14:48,975
No...

264
00:14:49,015 --> 00:14:51,285
Um... Well...

265
00:14:52,685 --> 00:14:54,485
Ah, Miwa!

266
00:14:57,955 --> 00:15:00,595
Hey, what do we do now?

267
00:15:00,895 --> 00:15:01,895
Huh?

268
00:15:04,545 --> 00:15:06,735
I just thought of a great idea.

269
00:15:09,465 --> 00:15:10,465
Uh...

270
00:15:11,265 --> 00:15:12,265
Um...

271
00:15:13,005 --> 00:15:17,105
Ah, the weather is really nice today...

272
00:15:18,475 --> 00:15:19,475
Yeah...

273
00:15:19,625 --> 00:15:21,515
- It really is...
- Yeah...

274
00:15:24,971 --> 00:15:26,825
[Light Music Group]

275
00:15:26,945 --> 00:15:27,945
That's weird.

276
00:15:28,355 --> 00:15:30,255
Looks like no one else is here yet?

277
00:15:33,855 --> 00:15:35,125
Huh? What?

278
00:15:35,785 --> 00:15:41,165
This is the 'You Can't Leave
Until You Make Up' room.

279
00:15:41,435 --> 00:15:42,435
Huh?

280
00:15:42,505 --> 00:15:46,305
So that's the deal.
Alright, good luck.

281
00:15:46,875 --> 00:15:48,304
What?

282
00:15:48,305 --> 00:15:50,605
Wait...

283
00:15:52,475 --> 00:15:54,915
Go get 'em!

284
00:15:54,945 --> 00:15:56,585
This is your great idea?

285
00:15:56,785 --> 00:16:00,855
Hey, don't press yourselves so close.

286
00:16:00,915 --> 00:16:02,815
Are they idiots?

287
00:16:03,565 --> 00:16:05,285
What on earth are they thinking?

288
00:16:17,605 --> 00:16:18,605
Miwa.

289
00:16:19,025 --> 00:16:20,025
Um...

290
00:16:20,885 --> 00:16:22,675
You're still mad, aren't you?

291
00:16:22,945 --> 00:16:23,975
About yesterday.

292
00:16:25,875 --> 00:16:26,875
No.

293
00:16:28,115 --> 00:16:29,285
I'm not mad.

294
00:16:29,945 --> 00:16:31,415
Liar.

295
00:16:33,865 --> 00:16:38,755
Of course, it still hurt.

296
00:16:39,965 --> 00:16:40,965
But...

297
00:16:42,225 --> 00:16:46,595
Since we're dating, having one or two
things you don't like about the other person

298
00:16:46,895 --> 00:16:49,395
is pretty normal, isn't it?

299
00:16:51,335 --> 00:16:52,725
If anything,

300
00:16:53,335 --> 00:16:57,305
on our anniversary,

301
00:16:58,185 --> 00:17:05,285
did I hurt Saeko's feelings and pride?

302
00:17:05,515 --> 00:17:08,015
What are you talking
about? You're overthinking it.

303
00:17:09,755 --> 00:17:10,925
I...

304
00:17:11,355 --> 00:17:14,625
If Saeko wants to do it,
I'll do my best.

305
00:17:15,065 --> 00:17:18,195
Huh? What are you saying?
What kind of declaration is that?

306
00:17:18,411 --> 00:17:20,151
I've already mentally prepared myself.

307
00:17:20,935 --> 00:17:22,775
If it's for Saeko, I'm
willing to do anything.

308
00:17:25,935 --> 00:17:27,735
Listen,

309
00:17:28,345 --> 00:17:32,505
how could I possibly sleep with a girl
making a face like that?

310
00:17:32,875 --> 00:17:33,875
Hey.

311
00:17:34,745 --> 00:17:35,745
What?

312
00:17:36,025 --> 00:17:37,245
You look like an octopus.

313
00:17:37,985 --> 00:17:39,585
What octopus...

314
00:17:40,405 --> 00:17:42,685
I'm being completely serious here.

315
00:17:43,325 --> 00:17:47,685
Ah, is this what you hate about me?

316
00:17:48,525 --> 00:17:52,995
If I had to say, it's how you're
so careless about a lot of things.

317
00:17:53,195 --> 00:17:55,234
And how you get carried away so easily.

318
00:17:55,235 --> 00:17:57,565
That's so mean.

319
00:17:57,635 --> 00:18:00,204
And that flippant attitude of yours...

320
00:18:00,205 --> 00:18:00,935
Hey...

321
00:18:00,936 --> 00:18:03,976
Plus, you're totally unromantic. I
might actually really hate that about you.

322
00:18:06,275 --> 00:18:07,275
I...

323
00:18:08,905 --> 00:18:14,685
might still find you annoying
sometimes in the future.

324
00:18:15,315 --> 00:18:18,555
But... including all of that,

325
00:18:19,285 --> 00:18:20,355
Um... cu...

326
00:18:33,155 --> 00:18:35,105
I think you're cute.

327
00:18:36,305 --> 00:18:39,815
I think everything about you is cute.

328
00:18:43,415 --> 00:18:44,645
Liar.

329
00:18:45,315 --> 00:18:46,985
I said you're cute.

330
00:18:48,585 --> 00:18:49,725
Really cute.

331
00:19:01,835 --> 00:19:02,835
Oh...

332
00:19:04,365 --> 00:19:06,275
Oh my, oh my.
Don't mind us, just ignore us.

333
00:19:06,415 --> 00:19:07,995
Please continue.

334
00:19:08,015 --> 00:19:10,255
- Please, please, please.
- Like we could continue!

335
00:19:19,275 --> 00:19:20,655
Sorry to intrude.

336
00:19:21,055 --> 00:19:22,055
Whoa.

337
00:19:22,715 --> 00:19:24,255
You keep this place so clean.

338
00:19:25,275 --> 00:19:28,795
It feels pretty mature.

339
00:19:33,475 --> 00:19:34,475
Um...

340
00:19:38,135 --> 00:19:40,994
Do you want to just stay over tonight?

341
00:19:40,995 --> 00:19:42,834
Huh? Really?

342
00:19:42,835 --> 00:19:44,775
Awesome.

343
00:19:48,855 --> 00:19:50,845
That's not what I meant...

344
00:19:52,435 --> 00:19:53,435
Hm?

345
00:19:54,475 --> 00:19:59,185
I mean... if it's okay today,
do you want to do it...?

346
00:19:59,655 --> 00:20:00,655
Huh?

347
00:20:01,455 --> 00:20:04,665
Why so sudden?

348
00:20:05,055 --> 00:20:12,435
Because... didn't you say
everything about me is cute?

349
00:20:29,615 --> 00:20:31,325
Are you still scared after all?

350
00:20:35,295 --> 00:20:37,165
It's... it's weird, right?

351
00:20:37,825 --> 00:20:42,665
Even though I know there's
no need to be scared, but...

352
00:20:51,215 --> 00:20:52,215
Miwa.

353
00:20:52,655 --> 00:20:54,415
Do you even have a sex drive to begin with?

354
00:20:55,255 --> 00:20:56,255
What?

355
00:20:56,845 --> 00:20:58,984
You really are totally unromantic.

356
00:20:58,985 --> 00:21:01,915
No, this is more important
than romance, right?

357
00:21:01,975 --> 00:21:05,055
If you don't have a sex drive at all,
how could I possibly force you to do it?

358
00:21:13,595 --> 00:21:15,395
I do.

359
00:21:16,375 --> 00:21:18,435
To be honest, I really do.

360
00:21:18,715 --> 00:21:22,575
When we first started dating, I
wanted to sleep with you so badly.

361
00:21:23,315 --> 00:21:24,315
Wait.

362
00:21:25,775 --> 00:21:26,845
I said my piece.

363
00:21:27,895 --> 00:21:29,015
What about you, Miwa?

364
00:21:34,955 --> 00:21:37,355
It's... it's not like I have none at all.

365
00:21:38,555 --> 00:21:39,714
What does that mean?

366
00:21:39,715 --> 00:21:41,125
So you do have one?

367
00:21:41,355 --> 00:21:42,355
Huh?

368
00:21:42,555 --> 00:21:43,555
Hm?

369
00:21:47,965 --> 00:21:51,565
Actually, I'm scared of doing that...

370
00:21:51,865 --> 00:21:55,235
Partly because it's my first time.

371
00:21:56,375 --> 00:21:57,375
But...

372
00:21:59,215 --> 00:22:00,215
But?

373
00:22:01,275 --> 00:22:03,845
I'm afraid that once the switch is flipped,

374
00:22:04,345 --> 00:22:06,655
I won't be able to control myself at all...

375
00:22:08,285 --> 00:22:09,355
So I'm scared.

376
00:22:13,575 --> 00:22:15,055
That sounds so dirty.

377
00:22:15,355 --> 00:22:17,715
Jeez, I told you not
to say things like that.

378
00:22:18,295 --> 00:22:19,714
Where is this switch?

379
00:22:19,715 --> 00:22:21,195
Here? Here?

380
00:22:21,765 --> 00:22:23,004
Is it here?

381
00:22:23,005 --> 00:22:24,904
Wait, stop it.

382
00:22:24,905 --> 00:22:26,335
I said it tickles.

383
00:22:27,635 --> 00:22:29,305
Jeez, stop it already.

384
00:22:56,565 --> 00:22:57,605
Miwa.

385
00:22:59,065 --> 00:23:01,035
I want all of you.

386
00:23:03,455 --> 00:23:06,945
I want to make everything about Miwa
mine.

387
00:23:14,555 --> 00:23:15,555
Yeah...

388
00:23:17,595 --> 00:23:18,595
Okay.

389
00:23:37,175 --> 00:23:39,175
It's okay, Miwa, you don't have to move.

390
00:23:45,645 --> 00:23:48,315
(Next Episode Preview)
Miwa, do you get jealous?

391
00:23:49,885 --> 00:23:51,234
Don't you get envious?

392
00:23:51,235 --> 00:23:53,134
Hello. I'm an intense yet
straightforward person.

393
00:23:53,135 --> 00:23:55,225
You have to protect your own body.

394
00:23:55,255 --> 00:23:57,394
Why did you suddenly push me away?

395
00:23:57,395 --> 00:23:59,765
It's so nice that Miwa
can be so honest about it.
